   "(iii) Section B to be completed and considered during cleaning and Section C to be completed after cleaning.All 3 sections to be verified by signature.",
   "Section A -Description / Prior Tank Washing",
   "Does the cargo belong to “persistent floaters” as per MARPOL Annex II Reg.13.7.1.4 and provision 16.2.7 in column “o” of Ch.17 of IBC Code?",
   "Does ship navigate in “North West European waters” as per MARPOL Annex II Reg.13.9?",
   "If answer in BOTH previous checks is YES, apply prewash procedures as per MARPOL Annex II - Appendix VI.",
   "Has the E/R been informed before start operation?",
   "Is the O2 into cargo tanks less than 5%?",
   "Is the IGS continuously running?",
   "Have the cargo tanks positive pressure? (>100mmWg)?",
   "Are all floater type level gauges in secured position?",
   "If portable Butterworth machines are going to be used, have the electric continuity checked?",
   "If portable Butterworth machines going to be used, have ISGOTT & TSGC (as applicable) requirements been followed?",
   "Is proper equipment for sounding used (cotton lines with bronze rod or sonic tapes)?",
   "Is a RA duly completed?",
   "Consider safety and environmental regulations (MARPOL-P&A-SOLAS as applicable)",
   "Consider Particularly Sensitive Sea areas (PSSAs)",
   "Crew familiarized with tank cleaning operation, incl. standards as per TSG-C (as applicable).",
   "Use environment friendly detergents",
   "Is adequate deck watch for monitoring the tank cleaning operation?",
   "The cargo tanks to be cleaned and the cleaning sequence agreed",
   "Type of cargo to be cleaned from each tank and its characteristics. Cargo information sheets should be available so that personnel involved are familiar with the hazards",
   "Consider major risks during cleaning, i.e. toxicity, flammability, corrosiveness and reactivity",
   "The safety equipment and PPE to be available and ready for use throughout the operation and during connecting and disconnecting of hoses at the cargo manifold",
   "Cleaning instructions to be followed in each case",
   "Are the means of disposal of any cargo residues and the contaminated cleaning water available? The relevant slop tank must be specified in each case",
   "Precautions necessary to confirm that the cargo deck area is free from cargo vapours during tank washing and gas freeing operations",
   "Has the preparatory meeting carried out, compliance to the above checks discussed and all persons involved in the operation briefed by the responsible Officer, with roles explained?",
