   "[B] The fenders have been checked, are in good order and there is no possibility of metal to metal contact.",
   "[B] Adequate electrical insulating means are in place in the barge-to-ship connection.",
   "[B] All bunker hoses are in good condition and are appropriate for the service intended.",
   "[D] Ensure that appropriate personnel are aware of intention to debunker and emergency response actions.",
   "[D] Discuss tank sequence with Officers.",
   "[D] The operation has been pre-planned. All persons to take part in this operation have been briefed.",
   "[E] The barge is securely moored.",
   "[E] There is a safe means of access between the ship and barge/terminal.",
   "[E] Effective communications (main and alternative systems) have been established between Responsible Officers.",
   "[E] Backup System: Emergency Stop Signal:",
   "[E] C/E’s standing orders for bunkering are permanently posted at bunker manifold/ECR. The procedures clearly state who is in charge of the operations and the communications procedures that are to be adopted. Emergency stop instructions are also clearly stated.",
   "[E] Was the operation discussed/agreed with the barge/terminal staff in charge?",
   "[E] There is an effective watch on board the barge/ terminal and on the ship.",
   "[E] Fire hoses and fire-fighting equipment at the barge/terminal and ship are ready for immediate use.",
   "[E] All drains are effectively plugged and checked for tightness (incl. the drain system, if applicable). Drip trays are in position on decks around connections and bunker tank vents.",
   "[E] Initial line up has been checked independently and physically by 2 Officers and unused bunker connections are blanked and fully bolted.",
   "[E] Officer A (name/ rank/signature):",
